    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d232-a2">

                <pb facs="0585" n="563" sameAs="frus:frus1872p2v2/pg563"/>

                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 2 in No. 97.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">General Schenck to Earl Granville.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >London</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1872-06-01"><hi rendition="#italic">June</hi> 1,
                        1872</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">My Lord</hi>: I received an hour ago your note of
                    this date, in which you reply to the telegram of Mr. Fish, which I communicated
                    to you this morning, and inform me that Her Majesty’s Government decline to sign
                    a treaty of the character and with the arrangement for the future, suggested by
                    Mr. Fish, but repeat their readiness to extend the time for the Arbitrators to
                    meet at Geneva, for which purpose Sir Edward Thornton has full powers to sign a
                    treaty; or they are willing, you state, to concur in a joint application to the
                    Tribunal of Arbitration to adjourn their proceedings, which they are advised it
                    is within the competence of the Arbitrators to do upon such an application
                    without a fresh treaty.</p>
                <p>I have sent the full text of your note to Mr. Fish by telegraph.</p>
                <p>I have, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>ROBT. C. SCHENCK.</signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
